# cw155, the doorway soap hand (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 2: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle cw155
revision 2
state ready
dialect coldwater
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for tn_lf_thistle_downcombe
written_by claude-codex-cw-2
title the doorway soap hand
fits stage=adult|old
prefers talk=plain
traits temper=calm talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=sly piety=ordinary drive=content
quirk chooses_a_seat_with_the_door_in_view
likes smoked_eel wrestling full_larder summer_evenings
dislikes waiting salt_wind
fears a_pan_of_soap_lost_to_a_careless_boil an_empty_larder_in_winter
hopes a_cupboard_full_before_frost an_evening_free_of_queues
topics work +0.5 home +0.4 food +0.3 pastimes +0.2
styles comfort=direct gossip=reluctant refuse=plain tease=dry
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# watches the #door# from a #bench#, judges a #boil# by its smell, and keeps a #loaf# in the #cupboard#.

words
oath! = Pan and paddle | By the open doorway
saying! = Count the loaves before the frost | Leave the doorway in sight
door = door | open door
doorway = doorway | house doorway
bench = bench | low bench
seat = seat | corner seat
back = back | turned back
window = window | narrow window
latch = latch | iron latch
cupboard = cupboard | food cupboard
larder = larder | full larder
loaf = loaf | fresh loaf
loaves = loaves | fresh loaves
bread = bread | bread heel
eel = eel | smoked eel
plate = plate | supper plate
supper = supper | evening meal
pan = pan | boiling pan
paddle = paddle | long paddle
soap = soap | plain soap
boil = boil | slow boil
lye = lye | lye water
ash = ash | clean ash
heat = heat | steady heat
steam = steam | sharp steam
batch = batch | soap batch
bar = bar | soap bar
bars = bars | soap bars
rack = rack | drying rack
hand = hand | working hand
hands = hands | working hands
work = work | boiling house work
house = house | shared house
child = child | grown child
neighbour = neighbour | near neighbour
visitor = visitor | unexpected visitor
road = road | High Road
city = city | Ridgemere
shop = shop | town shop
merchant = merchant | passing merchant
price = price | raised price
pay = pay | small pay
coin = coin | last coin
queue = queue | long queue
green = green | village green
bout = bout | wrestling bout
grip = grip | careful grip
summer = summer | late summer
wind = wind | lake wind
lake = lake | Glasswater
shore = shore | lakeshore
morning = morning | early morning
evening = evening | long evening
winter = winter | hard winter
fire = fire | low fire
water = water | lake water
cup = cup | small cup
hour = hour | full hour
silence = silence | welcome silence
letter = letter | folded letter
table = table | supper table
floor = floor | wooden floor
shutter = shutter | window shutter
sun = sun | low sun
day = day | long day

any
opinion @1 church against 1 : I can spare a #coin# for a hungry #neighbour#. | The collection #plate# travels faster than the help.
opinion @1 city against 1 : In the #city# nobody leaves a clear path to the #door#. | I prefer a room where faces stay known.
opinion @1 houses against 1 : Their #bench# has space until someone from our #house# comes near it. | I have stopped asking for a welcome.
opinion @1 merchants against 2 : The #price# of #bread# rises though my #pay# has barely moved. | A #merchant# can call that fair from a full #larder#.
opinion @1 newcomers against 1 : Let a #visitor# show some #work# before claiming a place in the #queue#. | I will judge the #hands#, not the tale.
opinion @1 watch against 1 : The watch counts who enters my #door# more closely than it counts missing #coin#. | They may start with the #road#.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : A #bout# on the #green# is worth seeing. | I still leave before the shouting starts.
opinion @1 times against 1 : Each #winter# seems to take another #loaf# from the #cupboard#. | Someone ought to count what remains.
line @1 greet : #greet#. That #seat# keeps the #doorway# in view. | #greet#. The #batch# is cooling.
line @2 greet [pair.band=friends|family] : Take the #bench# beside me; I kept a #plate#. | You know where the #cupboard# is.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : The #pan# was hot before the #morning# light. | #greet#. I have already fed the #fire#.
line @1 greet.return : The #soap# has yet to set since your last visit. | The #door# is open again, then.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Step into the light beside the #door#. | There is #bread# in the #cupboard# for kin.
line @1 again.open : The #lye# needs another stir. | Are we still counting that #price#?
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I must lift the #pan# from the #heat#. | Mind the #door# when you leave.
line @1 farewell.return : I can keep the better #seat# another #evening#. | Come before the #supper# is gone.
line @1 react.news : Speak while I stir; I hear you. | Start with who was at the #door#.
line @1 react.news.new : No one in this #house# brought me that word. | Was the word brought from the #road#?
line @1 react.news.known : I heard the edge of it at the #shop#. | There is more to the matter, I gather.
line @1 react.news.doubt : Show me where the story begins. | Let my #hands# test the claim first.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : Sit down. I can mind the #fire# while you rest. | Leave the #pan# to me; give yourself an #hour#.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : That calls for the good #plate#. | A fresh #loaf# would suit the occasion.
line @1 answer.how : My #pan# has behaved and the #larder# has a little left. | The #summer# #evening# suits me.
line @1 answer.how.busy [self.working=yes] : This #batch# needs steady stirring. | I cannot leave the #lye# alone.
line @1 ask.how : Did the climb along the #road# tire you? | Is your #house# fed today?
line @1 sympathise : I will leave this #seat# for you. | We can keep #silence# until you want company.
line @1 reassure : The #batch# can be started again. | A short delay will not empty every shelf.
line @1 decline : No. I cannot spare another #hour# standing in a #queue#. | I have the #pan# to watch.
line @1 accept_decline : Then leave the matter by the #door#. | Understood. Save the rest for another visit.
line @1 thank : You saved me a place in the #queue#. | That #bread# came at the right time.
line @1 deflect_thanks : My #hands# were free for a moment. | It was only one #loaf#.
line @1 preclose : The #soap# will set if I linger. | I need to see what is left in the #cupboard#.
line @1 tease [pair.band=friends] : That #bench# could throw you on a good day. | Your #paddle# has been resting more than you.
line @1 ack : #bc_right#. Set it by the #rack#. | #bc_fair_enough#. The #door# stays in my sight.
line @1 give.advice : Keep the #pan# at a low #heat# when the #lye# goes in. | Choose a #seat# with a view of whoever enters.
line @1 warn [world.bandits=near] : Keep to the lit #road# after dark. | I would travel with a #neighbour#.
scene back_to_door
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I take the #seat# facing the #door# even in my own #house#. | Seeing a #visitor# arrive lets me choose my words.
b : Does that make you uneasy? | Is the corner seat better?
a : Only when I cannot see the #latch#. | Better than a surprise at my #back#.

scene pan_temperature
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #soap# #batch# turns harsh if the #heat# climbs too fast. | I watch the #steam# and ease the #fire#.
b : Can you smell the change? | What if it boils over?
a : Before I see it. | Then the #floor# gets my whole #hour#.

scene ash_sieving
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fine #ash# makes cleaner #lye# when I sieve it. | A gritty #bar# tells on a careless #hand#.
b : Does it take long? | Can you fix a rough batch?
a : Long enough to do it properly. | Sometimes, before it sets.

scene drying_rack
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The #bars# rest on a #rack# with air between them. | Stack them close and the middles stay soft.
b : How many fit there? | Who checks them?
a : As many as I can lift safely. | I do, after the #morning# #boil#.

scene soap_skin
when topic=work
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Soap stings a cracked #hand# worse than #wind# off the #lake#. | I wrap my fingers before lifting the #paddle#.
b : Do you stop working? | Does that help?
a : Only if I must. | It keeps the #lye# out.

scene cupboard_count
when topic=home
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I count the #loaves# before promising anyone #supper#. | A full #larder# lasts longer when you know what is in it.
b : Do you write it down? | Is there enough tonight?
a : I remember each shelf. | There is #bread# for one more.

scene eel_supper
when topic=food
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Smoked #eel# keeps a place at my #table# when the #shop# has little else. | I cut thin pieces and leave the last for a late worker.
b : Do you warm the #eel# twice? | Who comes home late?
a : Just enough to warm it. | Someone from the boiling #house#.

scene summer_door
when topic=weather here.season=summer
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : In #summer# I sit where the #door# lets in the #evening# air. | I can hear the #green# without joining every argument.
b : Do you go out at all? | Is the air cool?
a : For a fair #bout#. | After the #sun# drops.

scene waiting_queue
when topic=prices
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #queue# at the #shop# swallowed my whole #morning#. | The #price# had risen by the time I reached the counter.
b : Did you buy anything? | Did you complain?
a : A smaller #loaf#. | Plainly, and to the right person.

scene quiet_bout
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I like a wrestling #bout# where both wrestlers know when to yield. | Noise among the watchers on the #green# adds nothing.
b : Do you wrestle now? | Who taught you?
a : When the #work# leaves my #hands# free. | A patient #neighbour#.

scene salt_wind
when topic=weather
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A sharp #wind# off the #shore# puts salt in my mouth. | It also dries the #soap# too quickly near the #window#.
b : Can you close it? | Does it ruin the bars?
a : I pull the #shutter# in. | If nobody notices in time.

scene empty_bench
when topic=memories
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Once a hall had an empty #bench# until my #work# clothes came through the #door#. | Then someone said the places were taken.
b : Were they? | What did you do?
a : I saw the open wood. | I went where I was welcome.

scene shared_house
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A shared #house# makes every #cupboard# #latch# somebody's concern. | I keep my #bread# together and say what is mine.
b : Do people quarrel? | Is there room to eat?
a : Less when I speak early. | Around one #table#.

scene child_plate
when topic=family
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I set aside a #plate# before the #pan# is clean. | A grown #child# can still arrive hungry.
b : Do you know when? | What do you leave?
a : Rarely. | The better piece of #eel#.

scene road_letter
when topic=travel
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : A #letter# can cross the #road# while I stay by the #boil#. | I keep it folded beside the #larder# key.
b : How often do you unfold it? | Does it bring good news?
a : More than I admit. | Enough to keep it dry.

scene chapel_plate
when topic=faith
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : I have watched a #plate# pass round the chapel faster than #bread# reached a poor #house#. | I still give when I know who will eat.
b : Do you attend? | Who receives your help?
a : On a quiet #morning#. | The #neighbour# I can see.

scene winter_stock
when topic=food here.season=winter
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Before #winter# I put #bars# of #soap# away and count every #loaf#. | A sealed #cupboard# keeps both dry.
b : Is that enough? | What about visitors?
a : For a short frost. | I offer #supper# when I can.

story scorched_batch [topic=work self.age>=18]
  : I once turned my #back# on a #pan# to answer someone at the #door#.
  : The #heat# climbed and the #batch# took on a burned edge.
  b : One distraction was enough. Could you save it?
  : I cooled it and kept the useful #bars# apart.

story withheld_seat [topic=home self.age>=18]
  : I entered a hall and chose a #bench# with the #door# in sight.
  : A stranger claimed every place was spoken for, though no one else came.
  b : That was unkind. Did you stay?
  : I found another room and kept my own company.

story last_eel [topic=food self.age>=18]
  : I saved the final piece of smoked #eel# for a late #hand#.
  : The #supper# hour passed, but the #door# opened after the #fire# sank low.
  ask : Was it still good?
  b : A thoughtful meal.
  : Warmed by the coals, and welcome.

rule @bark_pan
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Lower the #heat# before the #lye# goes in. | That #pan# needs another turn.

rule @bark_door
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 9h
say Leave the #door# clear. | I will take the #seat# facing the entrance.

rule @bark_larder
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 10h
say One more #loaf# behind the #latch#. | The #cupboard# can carry us another #day#.

rule @bark_green
when concept=bark here.day=festival
does aside
cooldown 11h
say A quiet #bout# is worth the walk. | The crowd on the #green# reaches this #bench#.

dlg @1 resident.hub : #greet#. The #soap# is cooling; speak while I watch the #door#. | #greet#. Pull that #bench# closer to the #door#.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : Back again? The #batch# held its shape. | I saved the corner #seat# if you need it.
dlg @1 resident.job : I work the #pan# at the boiling house. | Soap needs #lye#, #heat#, and a patient #hand#.
dlg @1 resident.bye : #farewell#. The #rack# wants my attention. | #saying.capitalize#. Mind your step outside.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you make the soap? -> soap
node soap
say First I sift the #ash# for #lye#, then keep the #boil# gentle. The #bars# dry apart on a #rack#.
free
choice Why face the doorway? -> seat
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node seat
say From this #bench# I see who comes in and can finish my thought before speaking to them.
choice Back to the soap. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye


grown
line @1 greet : #greet#. The #pan# is nearly ready. | #greet#. Choose the #seat# opposite mine.
line @1 farewell : #farewell#. I will check the #rack#. | The #door# will stay open until #supper#.
